'''Els Aiguamolls''' ({{lang|ca|Els Aiguamolls}}, Volisanian for "the wetlands") is a [[comarca]] on the [[Shendan Ocean]] coast of [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. It is the fourth comarca of Estret, situated immediately north of the [[Sant Cristòfor (comarca)|Sant Cristòfor]] comarca, and forms part of the northern suburban belt of the [[Sant Cristòfor]] metropolitan area. The comarca had a population of 1,665,000 in 2026 and an area of 679 km², giving it a population density of 2,452/km² — the highest of any comarca in Estret Province. The comarca seat is [[Vilanova, Estret|Vilanova]], the largest municipality with a population of 374,420.

The comarca is named for the extensive coastal wetlands and marshes that dominate its Shendan shoreline. These wetlands, protected within the [[Parc Nacional de la Marjal]], constitute one of the most significant ecological areas on the Balboan isthmus. Inland, the comarca transitions into densely developed suburban residential communities that function primarily as bedroom settlements for Sant Cristòfor, connected to the capital by [[CristoCarril]] [[Line E (CristoCarril)|Line E]] commuter rail and the [[Expressway 1 (Balboa)|E1 expressway]].

== Etymology ==

The name ''Els Aiguamolls'' derives from Volisanian ''aiguamolls'', meaning "wetlands" or "marshlands," referring to the extensive coastal marshes that characterise the comarca's Shendan shoreline. The name was applied to the administrative district during the Volisanian colonial period and has been retained as the comarca designation in the modern provincial subdivision system.

== Geography ==

Els Aiguamolls occupies the central Shendan coastal plain of Estret Province, immediately north of the Sant Cristòfor comarca. It is bounded by the [[Riu Llobregat]] to the south, which separates it from the [[Sant Cristòfor (comarca)|Sant Cristòfor]] comarca; the [[Serralada d'Estret]] to the east, which separates it from the [[L'Estany (comarca)|L'Estany]] comarca; an administrative boundary with the [[Les Planes (comarca)|Les Planes]] comarca to the north; and the [[Shendan Ocean]] to the west. The comarca has a total area of 679 km².

The Shendan coastal plain in this area is flat and low-lying, with elevations rarely exceeding 20 metres above sea level. The shoreline is characterised by extensive marshes, tidal flats, and mangrove forests, particularly in the southern and central portions of the coast. Several small rivers descend from the Serralada d'Estret and flow westward through the comarca to the Shendan Ocean, including the Riu Llobregat along the southern border and smaller watercourses that drain the interior.

Inland, the terrain rises gently toward the Serralada d'Estret in the east, where elevations reach approximately 100–150 metres at the comarca's eastern boundary. The transitional zone between the coastal plain and the hills is the primary area of suburban residential development. Off the northern Shendan coast lie a small archipelago of three islands — [[Sant Miquel, Estret|Sant Miquel]], [[Illa de Fora, Estret|Illa de Fora]], and [[Illa dels Ocells, Estret|Illa dels Ocells]] — forming the northernmost municipalities of the comarca.

=== Wetlands ===

{{main|Parc Nacional de la Marjal}}

The coastal wetlands of Els Aiguamolls comprise approximately 80 km² of tidal marshes, mangrove forests, and shallow lagoons along the comarca's Shendan shoreline. The wetlands are protected within the [[Parc Nacional de la Marjal]] (Marshland National Park), designated in 1956 during the [[International Mandate of Sant Cristòfor]] and one of the oldest national park designations in Balboa.

The park encompasses the largest remaining contiguous wetland ecosystem on the Shendan coast of the isthmus. The marshes are fed by seasonal freshwater inflow from the Serralada d'Estret watercourses and by tidal exchange with the Shendan Ocean, creating a brackish environment that supports extensive mangrove forests dominated by {{w|Rhizophora mangle|red mangrove}} and {{w|Avicennia germinans|black mangrove}}. The wetlands serve as a critical nursery habitat for commercially important fish and crustacean species and support large populations of resident and migratory waterfowl, wading birds, and seabirds.

The park is managed by the Balboan National Parks Service and is accessible to visitors via boardwalk trails and guided boat tours operating from the coastal settlement of [[Les Salines, Estret|Les Salines]]. The Parc Nacional de la Marjal was designated a {{w|Ramsar site|wetland of international importance}} in 1998.

=== Climate ===

Els Aiguamolls has a {{w|tropical monsoon climate}} with a pronounced wet season from May to December and a dry season from January to April. Annual rainfall averages approximately 1,400–1,600 mm, higher than the Sant Cristòfor comarca to the south due to the proximity of the Serralada d'Estret, which generates orographic rainfall during the wet season. Temperatures are consistently warm, with average highs of 30–32 °C and average lows of 23–25 °C throughout the year. The coastal wetlands are subject to seasonal flooding during the peak wet season months of October and November.

